LASER_ASSESSOR_MANUAL = ("The Laser assessor is your main instrument to interact with objects from afar. With it, you can ascertain if something is moving or static. It is also the primary way"
                        " you will lock onto objects. To use the laser, first turn it on either with the button labeled [PWR] in the laser assessor panel, or hit 'i' on your keyboard. Next you "
                        "can use the arrow buttons in the panel, or your arrow keys to move the laser. The Radar screen is very useful in using the laser from far away. To lock onto an object"
                        " either hit the [LOCK] button in the panel, or hit the space bar")
MISSILE_MANUAL = ("Missiles are your main weapon. They automatically avoid asteroids and cannot be defeated except by another missile. To use the missile, first you must have the beam of the "
                  "laser assessor on your target (locking it is optional, but keeps the beam on it). To fire the missile, either click on the button labeled [FIRE MSL] or hit 'p' on your keyboard."
                  " If you are locked by an enemy and they fire a missile at you, your screen will flash red. To defeat the missile, you must acquire a lock on the missile with your laser assessor and fire at it. The "
                  "radar is exceptionally useful for this.")
DECOY_MANUAL = ("Decoys are a deployable dummy drone that can be used to defeat enemy instruments. If you suspect that an enemy is about to discover you, you can deploy a decoy to throw them off of"
                " your trail. To use a decoy, press the button labeled [DECOY] or hit 'left-alt' on your keyboard. THey have a limited lifespan of about 60 seconds before they disappear.")
BLINK_DRIVE_MANUAL = ("The blink drive is a short range ftl jump that functionally teleports your ship to a random point somewhere in the engagement space. Be warned, it creates a large detectable "
                      "signature and uses a significant amount of fuel. You can use this to defeat a missile, or quickly reposition if you are being collapsed on. To use the blink drive, press "
                      "the button labeled [BLINK] or hit 't' on your keyboard. Note: YOu cannot blink if you have less than 50 fuel")
INERT_DAMPENER_MANUAL = ("The inertial dampening is an automated system that slows the ship down slowly when the ship is not using its thrusters. To toggle the inertial dampener, press the button "
                         "labeled [INERT DAMP] or hit 'g' on your keyboard.")
RADAR_MANUAL = ("The radar is an instrument that detects solid objects and displays them on the radar panel. It sweeps in a circle around the player. Radar cannot see through objects, so for example "
                "an enemy can hide behind an asteroid to defeat the radar sweep. To use the radar, press the button labeled [SWEEP] on the radar panel "
                "or hit 'r' on your keyboard. You can see the laser assessor on the radar panel, as well as direction indicators for the deep field scanner if it is turned on.")
PROX_MANUAL = "The proximity scanner is a simple, low power scanner that detects and adds objects that are close by to the tac map. It produces a very small albeit detectable signature."

DEEP_FIELD_SCANNER_MANUAL = ("The deep field scanner is an instrument used to detect movement in any given direction relative to the ship. For example, if the deep field scanner is pointed north"
                             " and then run, it will report whether an enemy ship or decoy north of your position is moving, and roughly how far away the nearest one is. "
                             "The range is only an estimate, off by as much as 20% either way, so scan again to refine it. It cannot provide headings or exact locations, and it "
                             "cannot tell a ship from a decoy. Be advised, any ship caught in the sweep is warned that it was scanned. To use the Deep field scanner, first turn it on by pressing the "
                             "[PWR] button in it's panel, or hit 'k' on the keyboard.  Then use the arrow buttons "
                             "in the panel or use the up and down arrow keys on your keyboard to change direction. The direction is indicated both in the ship window and the radar screen. To scan "
                             "press the button labeled [RUN SCAN] or hit 'o' on your keyboard. ")
TACTICAL_MAP_MANUAL = ("The tactical map is a map of the entire engagement space. It is useful for determining where to deploy drones and other instruments. To use the tactical map, hit 'm' "
                      "on your keyboard. It will only add objects to the map if the proximity scanner is running. Note: bjects slowly decay and fade on the "
                       "map. This is due to memory limitations that will be addressed in build 1.6.7.5b. Last, you can add markers to the map to help you remember details, like the location of "
                       "specific special asteroids, or "
                       "the general area of an enemy.")
FUEL_MANUAL = ("Fuel is your ships power source. All instruments and actions use some amount of power. Using many instruments at the same time will cause considerable draw on the remaining fuel. Draw "
               "is simply the amount of power that you are using at that moment. If you run out of fuel, you will still be able to move and perform certain actions, but they will be considerably "
               "degraded. For example, you will not be able to move very fast, you will not be able to blink, and you will not be able to use more than one instrument at a time. To refuel, find a "
               "asteroid of the type: [ICY] and use the mining subsystem to harvest fuel")
ASTEROID_MANUAL = "Asteroids are the most common objects in the engagement space. Be careful not to run into them as is the almost gauranteed destruction of your drone."
MATERIAL_ASSESSOR_MANUAL = ("The Material assessor is a scanner that is used in conjunction with the laser assessor to determine the composition of an object. It can be used to find an enemy who is "
                            "hiding among asteroids. It is also useful as a prospecting implement to find icy asteroids to refill your fuel with, or metallic asteroids to build new missiles with. To"
                            " use the material assessor, first make sure that the laser is shining on an object. It does not need to be locked on. Then either hit the button labeled [SCAN] in the "
                            "material assessor panel, or hit 'n' on your keyboard. Note: The farther away something is from you, the longer it takes to scan that object. Running the scan consumes a "
                            "small amount of power.")